1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,996
When Nvidia's CEO quit,

2
00:00:01,996 --> 00:00:03,215
the stock fell as much as

3
00:00:03,215 --> 00:00:05,489
fourteen percent in a single day.

4
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,116
When the board brought him back,

5
00:00:07,116 --> 00:00:09,378
it closed thirty-one percent higher.

6
00:00:09,589 --> 00:00:11,644
A company worth trillions of dollars,

7
00:00:11,644 --> 00:00:13,302
swinging on one man.

8
00:00:13,699 --> 00:00:14,431
The next day,

9
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:15,743
it slipped six percent,

10
00:00:15,743 --> 00:00:17,540
as the excitement faded.

11
00:00:17,937 --> 00:00:19,760
Here's what that tells you: this

12
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,791
market isn't just betting on AI.

13
00:00:21,791 --> 00:00:23,010
It's betting on a handful of

14
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:23,833
people.

15
00:00:23,974 --> 00:00:25,147
So what happens when one of

16
00:00:25,147 --> 00:00:26,921
them walks away for good?

